    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d582">

                <pb facs="0700" n="658" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg658"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Lord
                        Lyons.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-07-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 1, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: Adverting to your note of the 24th
                    ultimo, in which, to the refusal of the custom-house authorities at New York to
                    grant a clearance to the brig John Freeman, with cattle on board, you ask for
                    information as to the grounds of the prohibition of the exportation of cattle. I
                    have the honor to enclose you the copy of a communication of yesterday,
                    addressed to this department by the Secretary of the Treasury.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be your very obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lord Lyons.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d582-a1.xml" xpointer="d582-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
